# Pull Request Information

- **PR #**: 422
- **URL**: https://github.com/epam/dmtools-dart/pull/422
- **Title**: gh-394 Parity round: live-ADO findings (project resolution, link queries, auto-save template, ADO PR comments)
- **Author**: ai-teammate
- **Branch**: `ai/gh-394` → `main`
- **State**: open
- **Files Changed**: 5
- **Additions**: +91
- **Deletions**: -12
- **Created**: 2026-10-16T19:24:01Z
- **Updated**: 2026-10-16T21:19:06Z

## PR Description

Closes #394
### What changed
Dart parity for live-ADO findings: WIQL `WorkItemLinks` results are now read, and `ado_create_work_item` rejects a numeric project id with a clear error.

### Key decisions
- `wiqlResponseIds` reads both `workItems` stubs and `workItemRelations` (source/target nodes), de-duplicated and order-preserving. Used by both the async `AdoClient.listWorkItems` and the sync `ado_list_work_items` path.
- Numeric project check fails fast with `ArgumentError` before any HTTP call, instead of ADO's `TF200016`.
- No Dart change for the auto-save template (JS-only; `cli_execute_command` runs the full line via a temp `/bin/sh` script, so quoted messages pass through) or for the verdict text (no Dart verdict builder exists).
- `DEFAULT_SCM=ado` is not a Dart SCM provider (`kScmProviders` = github, gitlab). Adding one is a feature, not parity, so it is left out and flagged below.
- Agents suite (item 5) not run: no agents submodule in this checkout.

### How to verify
```bash
dart test test/integrations/ado test/js/sync_tool_dispatch_test.dart   # 182 passed
dart analyze lib/src/integrations/ado lib/src/js/sync_tools/ado_sync_tools.dart
```

<details><summary>Flow</summary>

```mermaid
flowchart TD
  WIQL[WIQL response] --> F{workItems?}
  WIQL --> R{workItemRelations?}
  F --> IDS[wiqlResponseIds]
  R --> IDS
  IDS --> BATCH[batch GET wit/workitems]
```

</details>

